{
  "meta": {
    "templateCredsSetupCompleted": true
  },
  "name": "Sync Google Calendar events to Asana tasks",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "8fddc7f5-ed2c-4fa2-b250-15817aa4258f",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1264,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 608,
        "height": 928,
        "content": "## Sync Google Calendar events to Asana tasks\n\nWho's it for: teams that plan in Google Calendar but track work in Asana and want every event to appear as an Asana task automatically.\n\n### How it works\n1. Every hour the workflow loads your calendar events from the last 3 days to the next 2 weeks (configurable).\n2. Each event is matched against a sync log kept in an n8n data table.\n3. A new event creates an Asana task with the event times, attendees from your company as followers, and a pinned summary comment.\n4. A changed event updates its task. A cancelled or declined event deletes it.\n5. The sync log stores each event's Asana task ID and last-synced time, so nothing is duplicated.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a data table with three text columns: CalendarEventID, AsanaTaskID, LastSyncedUpdate.\n2. Select that table in the three Data Table nodes.\n3. Fill in the Set configuration node: calendar ID, Asana workspace and project IDs, company email domain, time zone and sync window.\n4. Connect your Google Calendar and Asana accounts, run once manually, then activate.\n\n### Customization\nChange the schedule, the sync window, or the comment wording in the two \"Prepare\" code nodes."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
